# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. .env is gitignored.
# docker compose reads .env automatically at `up` time.
# The sandbox stack (docker-compose.test.yml) reads this same file, so it
# authenticates with the same token and uses the same API keys. A running
# sandbox keeps the old values until its container is recreated:
# `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml up -d`.
#
# Claude Code auth = a long-lived `claude setup-token` in CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
# (required, below). This is the SAME token OpenClaw uses — personal-vault
# `anthropic/oauth-token` (setup-token, Max-subscription quota, ~365d TTL).
# It is the SOLE auth gate when set and does NOT self-refresh, so rotate it
# before its ~2027-07-31 expiry: `claude setup-token` on the mini -> paste
# here -> `docker compose up -d receipt-assistant` -> update the vault +
# `openclaw models auth paste-token`. The host bind mount at
# ~/Developer/receipt-assistant-data/claude/ is now only an escape-hatch
# (unset this var + `claude /login`). See the `setup` skill + docker-compose.yml.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Long-lived Claude setup-token (see note above). Get it from personal-vault
# anthropic/oauth-token; NEVER commit the value — .env is gitignored.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Recommended ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Passwords for the two restricted database roles. The server sets them on
# the roles at every boot; the server's own DATABASE_URL is not in either
# agent's environment. Unset falls back to a built-in development password
# (and a warning at boot). Generate each with `openssl rand -hex 24`.
#   receipts_agent — the extraction / re-extract agent logs in as this:
#                    writes only what the prompts write
#   receipts_ro    — the server runs the Ask model's SQL as this: SELECT only
# RECEIPTS_AGENT_DB_PASSWORD=
# RECEIPTS_RO_DB_PASSWORD=

# Password of the database owner (the `postgres` superuser the server
# connects as). Unset means the public default `postgres`, which the
# extraction agent's shell can use to walk around its restricted role.
# Hex only. On an EXISTING database, change the role before setting this,
# or the server cannot connect: CLAUDE.md, "Rotating the owner password".
# RECEIPTS_DB_OWNER_PASSWORD=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below has sensible defaults; only override when needed.

# Parallel receipt extraction jobs. Each job spawns a claude subprocess,
# so increasing this raises memory + API load. Default: 3.
# MAX_CLAUDE_CONCURRENCY=3

# Model both agents run. The compose files pin claude-sonnet-5; set this
# only to override that, and only with a full model id, never an alias like
# `sonnet`: the value is stamped verbatim on every extracted row
# (metadata.extraction.model), and an alias stops naming one model the day
# the CLI is bumped.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Wave 1 switches, read by both compose files (defaults shown). Nothing reads
# them until the run records ship. EXTRACTION_WRITER: agent_sql (the agent
# writes the ledger by psql) or server_apply (the server writes it from the
# agent's record). EXTRACTION_REPAIR_ROUNDS: 0-2, how often an invalid
# record goes back to the same session.
# EXTRACTION_WRITER=agent_sql
# EXTRACTION_REPAIR_ROUNDS=1

# Google Maps API key. Used by the extraction agent (claude -p inside the
# container) to call Geocoding + Places APIs during Phase 3 of extraction.
# The agent skips geocoding silently when this is unset.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# HTTP server port. Default 3000. Also update the `ports:` mapping in
# docker-compose.yml if you change this.
# PORT=3000

# logo.dev API keys (#101 Phase 2 brand-icon acquisition). Obtain both
# from the logo.dev dashboard. The publishable key (pk_…) goes into
# img.logo.dev URLs; the secret key (sk_…) authorizes api.logo.dev/search.
# Phase 4b uses search-first against api.logo.dev to avoid the "any
# unknown domain returns a generated first-letter PNG" bug. The agent
# skips the logo.dev tier when either key is unset.
# LOGODEV_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# LOGODEV_SECRET_KEY=
